A Local Law to amend the New York city charter, in relation to an annual audit on domestic incident reports

Be it enacted by the Council as follows:


Section 1. Section 803 of chapter 34 of the New York city charter is amended by adding a new subdivision j to read as follows: 
j. No later than 180 days after the enactment of the local law that added this subdivision, and annually thereafter, the commissioner shall complete an audit of and submit a report to the council on domestic incident reports completed by the New York city police department. Such report shall include, at minimum: 
1. The total number of domestic incident reports completed, disaggregated by borough, council district, and police precinct; 
2. The percentage of domestic incident reports submitted with every mandatory field completed;
3. The fields most commonly left blank on domestic incident reports, and whether such fields are mandatory; 
4. The percentage of domestic incident reports indicating that hotline numbers, victim rights notices, or service referrals were provided to victims; 
5. The percentage of domestic incident reports submitted within 24 hours of the underlying incident; 
6. The percentage of domestic incident reports indicating the registry for orders of protection was checked; 
7. The percentage of domestic incident reports indicating an order of protection was in effect, disaggregated by form response, such as yes, no, refrain, or stay away; and 
8. Recommendations regarding improving the New York police department’s use of domestic incident reports and compliance with state law relating to such reports. 
§ 2.  This local law takes effect immediately. 

